{
  "kanji": "注",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 注\ntitle: pour, direct attention\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [チュウ]\nkunyomi: [そそ.ぐ, さ.す, つ.ぐ]\ndistractors: [主, 住, 洋]\n---\n\n# 注 — pour, direct attention\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 水 (as 氵, no. 85) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n注 can mean pouring liquid or directing attention toward something. It also occurs in words for notes and annotations. [注意](../words/注意.md) is the practical word for attention or caution.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** combine the visible water side 氵 ([水](水.md)) with [主](主.md) on the right. Imagine pouring water onto one main spot, then directing your attention to that spot. This is a mnemonic, not a claim about the character's origin.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; all source on/kun readings remain in the metadata.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| チュウ | on | [注意](../words/注意.md) ちゅうい — attention; 注文 ちゅうもん — order |\n| そそ.ぐ | kun | 注ぐ そそぐ — to pour |\n| さ.す | kun | 注す さす (to pour in; to add a drop), 目薬を注す めぐすりをさす (put in eye drops), 油を注す あぶらをさす (oil a mechanism) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [注意](../words/注意.md) ちゅうい — attention, caution\n- 注ぐ そそぐ — to pour\n- 注文 ちゅうもん — an order for something\n\n## Notes\n\nCompare [住](住.md): it has the same 主-shaped right side but a person side 亻 instead of water 氵.\nThe spelling 注ぐ also has other readings in Japanese; the example here specifically teaches そそぐ.\n",
